This product is an independent Windows port of the idea and design of MultiClaude for macOS
by Quentin Caron / Soma Labs (https://github.com/QuentinCar0n/multiclaude), licensed under the
Apache License 2.0. No source code, text or artwork from that project is included; the Windows
app was written separately in C#.

The Windows taskbar technique (per-window AppUserModelID tagging, re-adding the taskbar button,
and keeping profile data outside the Store app's virtualized AppData) follows the approach
documented by multi-claude by Thomas O.G. (https://github.com/thomasog/multi-claude), MIT License.

Claude is a trademark of Anthropic, PBC. This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by
Anthropic. It launches the official Claude desktop app and never modifies it. No Claude artwork
ships with it: profile icons are recolored at run time from the logo of the Claude app installed
on the user's computer.
